14559	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s2","entry":{"id":"review-593e0a07a57fc384f9fc7f36287fe914","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-23T10:32:30.373Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every s2 acceptance criterion (ac1-ac6 in DEF §6.2) is designed: the step-4 check (ac1/ac2), structured CLI output parsed directly with no model call (ac3), convertText with a cheap tier and a serial queue (ac4), callTool typed from Static of the schema (ac5), and the key-value cross-check (ac6).","evidence":"DEF.md:123-128 lists ac1-ac6. Each one maps to a contract in LLD §2 (executeTool step 4, callTool, convertText with keyValues) and to rows in §6's acceptance mapping. No non-goal (approval, hooks, family schemas) is built. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"DEF S002:FR001 ('A tool without a declared result shape cannot be registered') and FR004 ('Every tool declares the shape of its result') can be left unamended while this LLD keeps registration unchanged and makes outputSchema optional.","evidence":"DEF.md:44 states S002:FR001 and DEF.md:31 states FR004. The LLD does the opposite (outputSchema is optional, registration is unchanged) and says 'the DEF wording stays unamended'. The latest commit (f24619f3) records that the S002 FR001/FR004 DEF amendment is to be raised now, at the start of s2. The only s2 amendment on disk, AMD-b7a68147dcf72034-1, covers the HLD sc5 fields (ToolResult.failure, ToolFailure.original), not the DEF requirements. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, .insrc/artifacts/AMD-b7a68147dcf72034-1.json]","action":"Raise the DEF amendment for S002:FR001 and FR004 that narrows them to 'tools that code calls through callTool'. Reference it in §10 instead of leaving the DEF contradicted.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.3","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The LLD covers everything the HLD assigns to s2, including 'the way an input-to-tool mismatch is reported' and the typed input in the sc2 sketch.","evidence":"HLD.md:149 says s2 'includes the choice of schema language and the way an input-to-tool mismatch is reported'. The sc2 sketch at HLD.md:76 types the input as `input: ToolInput<T>`. The LLD's callTool takes an untyped `input: ToolInput`. The LLD notes in §7 that the executor does not validate input, but it designs neither input validation nor a failure kind for an input mismatch. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/HLD.md, src/daemon/tools/types.ts]","action":"Either design how an input mismatch is reported (validate against inputSchema and return kind 'rejected' or a named kind, with a typed input on callTool), or record a decision or amendment that drops it from s2's scope.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"executeTool looks the tool up, logs and auto-approves requiresApproval, and runs it in a try/catch. It does not validate input or output. An unknown id returns \"No tool registered for '<id>'\". Its only production caller is src/agent/read-only-tool-loop.ts:78.","evidence":"executor.ts:28-58 matches this, with error `No tool registered for '${toolId}'` at line 35. A grep for `executeTool(` finds only read-only-tool-loop.ts:78 and the definition. The comment at types.ts:104-107 claims input validation the executor does not do, as the LLD says. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/agent/read-only-tool-loop.ts, src/daemon/tools/types.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The tracker port has four failure kinds, and github.ts maps a timeout to 'unreachable' with the message 'timed out after N s'.","evidence":"port.ts:23 is `PortFailureKind = 'missing-tool' | 'missing-signin' | 'unreachable' | 'rejected'`. github.ts:76 is `new GhCommandError('unreachable', `gh timed out after ${GH_TIMEOUT_MS / 1000} s`)`. [files: src/workflow/tracker/port.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The reused validateAgainstSchema does not mutate the payload (removeAdditional off), caches compiled validators per schema object, and reports a schema it cannot compile without throwing. typebox is already a dependency, so Static<TSchema> is available.","evidence":"structured-output.ts:59-64 sets `removeAdditional: false, useDefaults: false`. Lines 89-93 catch a compile error and return `{ ok: false, errors: ['ajv.compile failed: …'] }`. package.json:36 has `@sinclair/typebox ^0.34.49`. One note: the shared instance is a plain `Ajv` (draft-07), not Ajv2020, so the alternative a1's text 'JSON Schema 2020-12' is slightly wrong. The executor also has to tell a compile failure from a mismatch by the 'ajv.compile failed' prefix. [files: src/agent/providers/structured-output.ts, package.json]","action":"Fix the 2020-12 wording. In the invalid-schema error path, say that it is detected by the 'ajv.compile failed' prefix.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The two new roles (tools.convert cheap, tools.convert.escalate mid) can be added as peripheral entries in the closed taxonomy, resolve through the RoleRouter like any other role, and are not clamped by the coreFloor.","evidence":"role-taxonomy.ts:82-92 already holds peripheral roles with defaultTier 'cheap' or 'mid'. role-router.ts:107-125 resolves the tier from roleTiers, then the descriptor's defaultTier, then applyCoreFloor. core-floor-guard.ts:116-117 passes peripheral roles through. [files: src/config/role-taxonomy.ts, src/analyze/context/role-router.ts, src/config/core-floor-guard.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"convertText(req: ConversionRequest<S>), with req = { toolId, rawText, schema, keyValues }, carries everything it needs to resolve the two roles' providers and to honour cancellation through deps.signal.","evidence":"`RoleRouter.resolveProviderForRole(role, cfg: AnalyzeConfig, repoPath?)` (role-router.ts:79) needs an AnalyzeConfig, and per-repo roleTiers need a repoPath (role-router.ts:99). Neither is in ConversionRequest, and the LLD says it 'adds no field to ToolDeps'. The cancellation error path ('deps.signal is aborted before the queue slot is taken…') and its test ('an aborted signal drops a queued conversion') depend on a signal that convertText never receives. The fake-RoleRouter test fixture also assumes an injection seam the signature lacks. [files: src/analyze/context/role-router.ts, src/daemon/tools/types.ts]","action":"Add the missing inputs to the contract: a router (or a provider resolver), the AnalyzeConfig, the repoPath and an optional AbortSignal, either as fields of ConversionRequest or as a second deps parameter. State where a tool gets the config from. Update the sc3 sketch amendment to match.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Adding optional failure to ToolResult and optional outputSchema to Tool needs no change at existing call sites: the agent loop reads only output, success and error.","evidence":"In types.ts:33-48 every ToolResult field except output, format and success is optional, and Tool (types.ts:96-152) has several optional fields already, so the additions compile without edits. read-only-tool-loop.ts:89-94 forwards the ToolResult from execute unchanged. [files: src/daemon/tools/types.ts, src/agent/read-only-tool-loop.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The tracker port's PortFailureKind and the unit-issue test that iterates its kinds stay unchanged. New kinds are mapped onto the four existing ones at the adapter.","evidence":"unit-issue.test.ts:390 iterates `['missing-tool','missing-signin','unreachable','rejected']`. The LLD leaves port.ts:23 as it is, and the mapping in §3.5 (timed-out→unreachable; conversion-failed, schema-mismatch and denied→rejected) needs no change to the stored shape. [files: src/workflow/tracker/__tests__/unit-issue.test.ts, src/workflow/tracker/port.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The additions are optional, and no stored record or older data has to change (no data rewrite).","evidence":"Tool and ToolResult are in-memory contracts (types.ts). executor.ts returns results without persisting them. The only behaviour change is the extra optional `failure` on error results; output, success and error keep their current text (executor.ts:31-36, 52-57). [files: src/daemon/tools/types.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The LLD does not redesign contracts owned by s1 (the hook stage, sc1) or s3 (approval, sc4). It owns only step 4, sc2, sc3 and sc5, and it raises the ApprovalDenial cross-Story dependency as an open question instead of defining it.","evidence":"HLD.md:147-149 gives s2 sc2, sc3 and sc5 and says 'It does not declare or read the approval class'. In the LLD, executeTool's precondition says steps 1-3 are not s2's. The executor.ts auto-approve line is left alone (s3 removes it). ApprovalDenial (HLD.md:114, owned by s3) is referenced only through the sc5 sketch (HLD.md:132), and the missing s2→s3 dependency is raised in §10. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/HLD.md]","action":"Settle the §10 ApprovalDenial question (declare the union in s2, or amend the dependency order) before the build, because s2 has no dependency on s3 (HLD.md:214).","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The per-attempt deadline can be built 'within withStructuredRetry': aborting a hung provider call counts as one failed attempt and the retries go on.","evidence":"structured-output.ts:215 has `if (err instanceof Error && err.name === 'AbortError') throw err;`, so an aborted call ends the whole retry helper instead of being retried. If the deadline is put in place as an AbortSignal on the provider call, as the LLD describes, the first timeout ends the conversion and no later attempt or escalation runs. That contradicts 'count the attempt as failed … and release the queue slot' and the retry budget. The same rethrow is what makes caller cancellation work, so the two cases need different handling. [files: src/agent/providers/structured-output.ts]","action":"State that a deadline abort is turned into a non-AbortError (for example a 'timed out' Error) inside the StructuredCall closure, so withStructuredRetry retries it. Only a caller cancellation should be rethrown as AbortError and mapped to 'cancelled'.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"An input too large for the cheap tier is detected and returned as 'retries-exhausted' with 'input too large', not truncated silently or resent.","evidence":"structured-output.ts:219 rethrows an InputTooLargeError without retrying, so convertText can catch it and map it to the stated failure. [files: src/agent/providers/structured-output.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion ac1-ac6 maps to at least one named test in a concrete test file.","evidence":"In LLD §6, ac1-ac6 each list tests in output-schema.test.ts, call-tool.integration.test.ts, convert-text.test.ts, call-tool.types.test.ts or convert-text.live.test.ts. These match DEF.md:123-128. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.2","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The ac5 compile-time tests in src/daemon/tools/__tests__/call-tool.types.test.ts use // @ts-expect-error lines that `npm run build` (tsc) checks.","evidence":"tsconfig.json:27-28 has `\"exclude\": [\"**/__tests__/**\"]`. The build script is `tsc && node copy-assets.mjs` (package.json:15), and tests run through `tsx --test`, which strips types without checking them. No tsconfig in the repo type-checks src/**/__tests__ (the only one there is a CLI fixture config). The @ts-expect-error assertions would never be evaluated, so ac5 would pass whether or not it holds. [files: tsconfig.json, package.json]","action":"Put the type-level assertions in a file tsc compiles (outside __tests__, for example a *.type-test.ts under src that the build includes), or add a test tsconfig and a `tsc -p` step that the validate gate runs. Then map ac5 to that.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"}],"counts":{"high":1,"med":4,"low":11,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-23T10:32:30.373Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
