10533	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s2","entry":{"id":"review-9f4bae718b7cdc54edae1fcf80c7b14e","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-23T10:40:43.389Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Keeping registration unchanged and making outputSchema optional (instead of DEF S002 FR001/FR004) follows a recorded upstream decision.","evidence":"docs/plans/tool-registry.md:94-98 'Decision: output schemas are required only for tools that code calls': callTool accepts only a schematized definition (compile-time guard), agent-only tools need no schema, and the section gives replacement DEF wording for S002:FR001/FR004. The DEF text itself is not amended yet; the LLD flags this in open question 2. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Before approval, raise or accept the S002 FR001/FR004 DEF amendment using the wording in tool-registry.md:98.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"callTool takes the tool definition object, not a string id, as the HLD decided.","evidence":"tool-registry.md:80 decision 3: 'The typed helper takes the tool definition object (callers import it), not a string id'. LLD 2.1 callTool<T extends TypedTool>(tool: T, ...) matches. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"executeTool today looks the tool up, returns 'No tool registered for <id>' for an unknown id, auto-approves gated tools, and runs execute inside a try/catch with no input validation, although the Tool.inputSchema comment says it validates.","evidence":"src/daemon/tools/executor.ts:28-58: getTool, then error `No tool registered for '${toolId}'`; log.warn '...auto-approving'; try { return await tool.execute } catch returns '[Tool failed] ...'. types.ts:103-108 says 'Schema validation is enforced by the executor', but the executor has no validation. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/types.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The only production caller of executeTool is src/agent/read-only-tool-loop.ts:78.","evidence":"Grep for 'executeTool(' in src finds only read-only-tool-loop.ts:78 and the definition in executor.ts:23. [files: src/agent/read-only-tool-loop.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The reused validateAgainstSchema runs ajv with removeAdditional off, caches compiled validators per schema object, and the design treats a schema compile failure as a distinct 'rejected' case.","evidence":"structured-output.ts:59-64 Ajv({allErrors:true, useDefaults:false, removeAdditional:false, strict:false}); :79-82 says validators are cached per schema object. :89-93 never throws on a compile failure: it returns {ok:false, errors:['ajv.compile failed: ...']}. The LLD covers this ('throws or reports a compile error'). The executor must recognise the 'ajv.compile failed' prefix to return 'rejected' rather than 'schema-mismatch'. [files: src/agent/providers/structured-output.ts]","action":"In the build, detect the compile failure by the 'ajv.compile failed:' error prefix, since the helper never throws.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"withStructuredRetry rethrows AbortError and InputTooLargeError at once and retries any other thrown error, so a deadline must be raised as an ordinary Error.","evidence":"structured-output.ts:212-229: 'if (err.name === 'AbortError') throw err; if (err.name === 'InputTooLargeError') throw err;' any other error becomes lastErrors and the loop continues. [files: src/agent/providers/structured-output.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.3","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"RoleRouter.resolveProviderForRole is synchronous, and typebox and ajv are already dependencies.","evidence":"role-router.ts:79 resolveProviderForRole(role, cfg, repoPath?): ResolvedProvider (not a Promise). package.json:36 '@sinclair/typebox': '^0.34.49', :41 'ajv': '^8.20.0'. [files: src/analyze/context/role-router.ts, package.json]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"'The two existing builders of ToolDeps' (driver.ts:1132, ollama.ts:686) are the complete inventory of production ToolDeps construction sites.","evidence":"Production code builds ToolDeps in at least two more places: src/workflow/code-review/grounding.ts:370 `const toolDeps: ToolDeps = { sessionId: 'code-review', repoPath, send: () => {}, requestId: 0 }` and src/workflow/runners/build/changed-files.ts:110 (the same literal), as well as ollama.ts:686. The field is optional, so nothing breaks at compile time. But these workflow-side builders have no conversion field, so once s4-s7 give them text-only tools those calls fail with 'no conversion provider configured'. [files: src/workflow/code-review/grounding.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/changed-files.ts, src/agent/providers/ollama.ts]","action":"Correct the inventory in 3.4 to list grounding.ts:370 and changed-files.ts:110, and say who (s7 or this Story) adds deps.conversion there.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The new roles can be added to the role taxonomy as peripheral entries with defaultTier cheap/mid; RoleId is an open string and the coreFloor applies only to critical roles.","evidence":"role-taxonomy.ts:31 `export type RoleId = string`; entries are { id, criticality, defaultTier } (e.g. :82 tracker.render.issueBody peripheral cheap). role-router.ts:108-125 takes the tier from roleTiers or descriptor.defaultTier, and applyCoreFloor passes peripheral roles through. [files: src/config/role-taxonomy.ts, src/analyze/context/role-router.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The tracker port keeps its four PortFailureKinds, and the stated mapping of timed-out to unreachable matches how github.ts maps a timeout today.","evidence":"port.ts:23 PortFailureKind = 'missing-tool' | 'missing-signin' | 'unreachable' | 'rejected'. github.ts:75-76 maps ETIMEDOUT/SIGTERM to new GhCommandError('unreachable', `gh timed out after ${GH_TIMEOUT_MS / 1000} s`). [files: src/workflow/tracker/port.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"All additions (Tool.outputSchema, ToolResult.failure, ToolDeps.conversion) are optional, so existing builtins and stored shapes are unaffected.","evidence":"types.ts:33-48 ToolResult and :50-81 ToolDeps already use optional '| undefined' fields. Adding optional fields keeps every existing literal valid under exactOptionalPropertyTypes. No persisted ToolResult store exists. [files: src/daemon/tools/types.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The Story stays out of s1 (hooks) and s3 (approval). It only declares a ToolDenialReason union that s3 reuses, and proposes it through an HLD amendment.","evidence":"LLD 2.2 preconditions leave steps 1-3 (resolve, approval, run) to the executor and s3, and the hook stage to s1. The caller-identity carrier (tool-registry.md:89 finding 4) is explicitly left to s1/s3. The denial union is additive, flagged as an sc5 fieldAdd amendment, and does not design the approval flow. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Cancellation and the per-attempt deadline are detectable: provider calls accept an AbortSignal, and the retry helper ends on AbortError.","evidence":"shared/types.ts:228-232 completeStructured(messages, schema, opts?: StructuredCompletionOpts); StructuredCompletionOpts carries signal?: AbortSignal (types.ts:103). structured-output.ts:215 rethrows AbortError, so the design's split (deadline as an ordinary Error, caller cancellation as AbortError) can be implemented. [files: src/shared/types.ts, src/agent/providers/structured-output.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion ac1-ac6 maps to a named test, and the ac5 type-level tests live in a file the build type-checks.","evidence":"Section 6 maps ac1-ac6 to tests in output-schema, call-tool, convert-text and call-tool.integration test files. tsconfig.json:27-28 excludes '**/__tests__/**', so placing call-tool.type-test.ts outside __tests__ is correct. Some mapped titles (e.g. 'the check runs before the result is returned to the caller') are not in the unit subject list; align them at build time. [files: tsconfig.json]","action":"Make the acceptance-mapping titles match the test titles that are actually written, so the validate-phase mapping resolves.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":1,"low":13,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-23T10:40:43.389Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
